00:48:33.080 --> 00:48:33.400
Yeah.

1007
00:48:33.560 --> 00:48:38.340
Just like, it was actually, to be there, really romantic.

1008
00:48:38.980 --> 00:48:40.060
You know, it was funny.

1009
00:48:40.220 --> 00:48:42.460
The gas station, it was just a front.

1010
00:48:42.680 --> 00:48:44.860
If you went in, it was like a fakey fake.

1011
00:48:45.080 --> 00:48:47.260
You go through the door and then you're just like looking at trees.

1012
00:48:47.260 --> 00:48:48.800
It didn't have a back or anything.

1013
00:48:49.560 --> 00:48:51.180
But it felt magical.

1014
00:48:51.360 --> 00:48:52.020
It did.

1015
00:48:52.200 --> 00:48:54.240
And it was so much fun to shoot that scene.

1016
00:48:54.360 --> 00:48:57.940
I mean, I feel like we got it on the first take and maybe we did a few.

1017
00:48:58.240 --> 00:49:01.880
But my memory is that we weren't there long, that we got it pretty early.

1018
00:49:02.160 --> 00:49:03.500
And it was a cool moment.

1019
00:49:03.660 --> 00:49:05.240
It's a really magical moment.

1020
00:49:05.820 --> 00:49:08.980
Well, when the gang is ready to weigh in again, Jim is late.

1021
00:49:09.260 --> 00:49:11.020
And then he shows up soaking wet.

1022
00:49:11.220 --> 00:49:12.300
And so happy.

1023
00:49:12.480 --> 00:49:13.220
So happy.

1024
00:49:13.940 --> 00:49:18.140
I was a little sad that they didn't get to spend the whole evening together after getting engaged.

1025
00:49:18.340 --> 00:49:20.420
I guess Pam just had to drive back to school.

1026
00:49:20.720 --> 00:49:21.300
I know.

1027
00:49:21.760 --> 00:49:22.940
But Jim is so happy.

1028
00:49:23.300 --> 00:49:26.060
Holly decides that this yoga guy is never going to call her.

1029
00:49:26.460 --> 00:49:28.220
And Michael says, you know what?

1030
00:49:28.300 --> 00:49:30.240
I'll buy the Counting Crows tickets from you.

1031
00:49:30.640 --> 00:49:32.080
And she's like, really?

1032
00:49:32.280 --> 00:49:36.360
Everybody thinks this is like going to lead to Michael offering to go with her.

1033
00:49:36.360 --> 00:49:38.040
I thought they were going to have a date.

1034
00:49:38.720 --> 00:49:39.160
No.

1035
00:49:39.580 --> 00:49:41.440
Michael rips up the tickets.

1036
00:49:41.440 --> 00:49:42.960
Like, gallantly.

1037
00:49:43.260 --> 00:49:44.860
Like, he's saving the day.

1038
00:49:45.080 --> 00:49:46.540
And she's confused.

1039
00:49:47.000 --> 00:49:49.120
We got some mail from Emily G.

1040
00:49:49.380 --> 00:49:49.680
Okay.

1041
00:49:49.800 --> 00:49:50.720
Here's what she said.

1042
00:49:50.940 --> 00:49:56.760
Having worked at several concert venues, I wanted to let you know that if you lose or damage your concert tickets,

1043
00:49:56.940 --> 00:50:02.340
you can go to a venue's box office with your photo ID and someone will reprint them for you.

1044
00:50:02.640 --> 00:50:03.160
Oh.

1045
00:50:03.400 --> 00:50:06.080
She said, I hope Holly knew that was an option.

1046
00:50:06.380 --> 00:50:07.740
Oh, that's good to know.

1047
00:50:08.020 --> 00:50:08.360
Yeah.

1048
00:50:08.640 --> 00:50:10.380
It didn't seem like Holly knew.

1049
00:50:10.380 --> 00:50:12.020
No, I didn't know.

1050
00:50:12.280 --> 00:50:13.360
Well, now we all know.

1051
00:50:13.360 --> 00:50:14.060
Now we all know.

1052
00:50:14.180 --> 00:50:14.940
Thank you, Emily.

1053
00:50:15.120 --> 00:50:15.380
Yeah.

1054
00:50:15.800 --> 00:50:22.640
In the end, Dunder Mifflin did not win the weight loss competition.

1055
00:50:23.220 --> 00:50:24.980
Stanley lost seven pounds.

1056
00:50:25.280 --> 00:50:25.640
Yeah.

1057
00:50:25.840 --> 00:50:28.020
He says he's going to take off five days anyway.

1058
00:50:28.320 --> 00:50:28.580
Yeah.

1059
00:50:28.920 --> 00:50:30.480
And now it's week eight.

1060
00:50:31.500 --> 00:50:35.100
Toby is on his fifth week in a hospital room in Costa Rica.

1061
00:50:35.100 --> 00:50:36.880
Oh, poor Toby, guys.

1062
00:50:37.100 --> 00:50:37.340
Remember?

1063
00:50:37.880 --> 00:50:41.320
Toby had his weird moment with Pam, so he moved to Costa Rica.

1064
00:50:41.740 --> 00:50:45.000
And on like his first day, or day, was it like day three?

1065
00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:45.120
Day three.

1066
00:50:45.120 --> 00:50:46.880
Day three, he went ziplining.

1067
00:50:47.280 --> 00:50:48.460
And he broke his neck.

1068
00:50:48.680 --> 00:50:48.920
Yeah.

1069
00:50:49.220 --> 00:50:51.000
He hasn't even been to the beach.

1070
00:50:51.560 --> 00:50:54.340
Did you notice what was playing on the TV in the hospital room?

1071
00:50:54.580 --> 00:50:55.240
Yes, I did.

1072
00:50:55.240 --> 00:50:58.540
It is the hug it out, bitch, episode of Entourage.

1073
00:50:59.180 --> 00:51:03.240
That is the episode of Entourage that Michael quotes in The Coup.

1074
00:51:03.520 --> 00:51:07.940
Well, I have a little location breakdown for you about Toby's hospital room.

1075
00:51:08.060 --> 00:51:08.680
Give it to me.

1076
00:51:08.880 --> 00:51:10.900
It was also filmed at USC.

1077
00:51:11.420 --> 00:51:11.900
Oh!

1078
00:51:12.140 --> 00:51:12.480
Yeah.

1079
00:51:12.580 --> 00:51:17.480
While they were there filming Pam's Art School, they used the USC television stage building.

1080
00:51:17.640 --> 00:51:21.580
And USC asked if eight of their film students could intern and help that day.

1081
00:51:21.760 --> 00:51:23.640
They had interns in all of the different departments.

1082
00:51:23.640 --> 00:51:26.520
And our crew said they did a phenomenal job.

1083
00:51:26.720 --> 00:51:28.140
That is so cool.

1084
00:51:28.340 --> 00:51:28.720
Mm-hmm.

1085
00:51:29.200 --> 00:51:35.980
Before we go, I just want to give a shout out to whoever the guy is in the bed next to Toby.

1086
00:51:36.520 --> 00:51:38.180
He was a background performer.

1087
00:51:38.440 --> 00:51:43.480
Angela, I tried so hard to figure out who this is because he is so funny.

1088
00:51:43.880 --> 00:51:50.660
He just stares into the camera the whole time Toby is talking.

1089
00:51:50.880 --> 00:51:52.100
It is so good.

1090
00:51:52.100 --> 00:51:53.920
I watched it three times.

1091
00:51:54.040 --> 00:52:00.220
I was like, how is this guy doing such a great job with no words?

1092
00:52:00.300 --> 00:52:01.400
I was so impressed.

1093
00:52:01.560 --> 00:52:02.920
We couldn't figure out who he was.

1094
00:52:03.020 --> 00:52:04.560
We reached out to several people.

1095
00:52:04.820 --> 00:52:05.260
Yes.

1096
00:52:05.440 --> 00:52:07.440
And I checked everywhere you can check.

1097
00:52:07.600 --> 00:52:09.240
He is uncredited in the episode.

1098
00:52:10.140 --> 00:52:11.040
Phenomenal job.

1099
00:52:11.280 --> 00:52:12.340
Way to crush it.

1100
00:52:12.700 --> 00:52:16.700
And you guys, that was weight loss part two.

1101
00:52:16.700 --> 00:52:21.000
Oh, there's so many folks to thank for helping us get this episode out to you.

1102
00:52:21.160 --> 00:52:26.680
First of all, our crew that participated in the DVD commentary, Randy Cordray, Michael Gallenberg,

1103
00:52:26.820 --> 00:52:32.320
Brian Whittle, Nick Carbone, Ben Patrick, Alicia Raycraft, Kelly Cantley, and Jake OuSt.

1104
00:52:32.820 --> 00:52:33.320
Amazing.

1105
00:52:33.600 --> 00:52:34.520
Best commentary.

1106
00:52:34.940 --> 00:52:38.180
Really such a good listen if you love behind-the-scenes information.

1107
00:52:38.180 --> 00:52:41.520
And James O'Carri for letting us bug you with questions.

1108
00:52:42.140 --> 00:52:42.980
Yeah, we did.

1109
00:52:43.060 --> 00:52:43.920
We did bug him.

1110
00:52:44.040 --> 00:52:44.540
We did.

1111
00:52:44.720 --> 00:52:45.460
And Joya Balfour.

1112
00:52:45.620 --> 00:52:46.140
Oh my gosh.

1113
00:52:46.140 --> 00:52:52.020
I'm so excited to share all of that NBC.com website stuff about Angela and Andy.

1114
00:52:52.200 --> 00:52:53.760
And then Greg Daniels.

1115
00:52:53.800 --> 00:52:54.160
Yes.

1116
00:52:54.160 --> 00:52:54.780
Thank you.

1117
00:52:54.940 --> 00:52:57.600
And also, Paul Feig for that audio clip.

1118
